                <pb facs="0033" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13976: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-18T12:00:00+08:00">February 18,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 18—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. My 77, February 15, noon. National Government in a mandate issued February 17
                    restored to Chang Hsueh Liang his civic rights of <pb facs="0034" n="27"
                        xml:id="pg27"/> which he had been deprived for 5 years by judgment of high
                    court martial of the Military Affairs Commission on December 31, 1936. Question
                    of restoration of former rank still unsettled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
